120 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 73 0 R
/E (Cybersecurity advice is often technical, scattered or difficult for beginners and older users to understand.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
121 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 73 0 R
/E (Example scenario: A user receives a message claiming that a bank account will be blocked unless a link is opened. CyberTab can help identify suspicious wording, explain why the message may be risky and suggest safe next steps without asking the user to share passwords, PINs or OTPs.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
122 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 73 0 R
/E (People increasingly rely on digital services, but scam messages, phishing links, fake websites, impersonation and misleading online offers can be difficult to recognize. Users may not know which warning signs to check, how to respond safely or where to report an incident. Information about prevention and reporting is also spread across different sources, which can create confusion at the moment help is needed.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
123 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 73 0 R
/E (CyberTab addresses this gap through a single, easy-to-use platform that combines scam-awareness guidance, AI-assisted explanations, a cybersecurity chatbot and a guided complaint-preparation workflow. It is designed to communicate in clear, non-technical language and support users in English, Hindi and Telugu.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
124 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 73 0 R
/E (Without accessible guidance, users may trust suspicious messages, click unsafe links, disclose confidential information or delay reporting an incident. A simple support platform can help users pause, assess warning signs, protect their accounts and find appropriate official reporting channels.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
