127 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 73 0 R
/E (Cybercrime and online fraud increasingly affect people who use digital payments, messaging apps, social media, shopping platforms and online services. Many users, especially students, parents, first-time internet users and older adults, may find it difficult to identify phishing attempts, impersonation, fake offers, fraudulent links and other suspicious activity. CyberTab aims to make basic cyber-safety guidance easier to understand and access through a simple, approachable interface.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
128 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 73 0 R
/E (The project uses AI to analyze user-submitted text or other supported scam-related content, explain warning signs and suggest practical safety steps. It also provides a conversational assistant for general cybersecurity questions and helps users organize incident information into a complaint draft when they explicitly request it. The project supports SDG 9 \(Industry, Innovation and Infrastructure\) through accessible digital innovation and SDG 16 \(Peace, Justice and Strong Institutions\) through awareness of reporting pathways and responsible digital participation.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
